      "description": "Client-observed read latency from the stress summary (`selects`, seconds, scaled to microseconds) overlaid on coordinator-observed read latency per node (`cassandra_client_request_latency_${percentile}_microseconds`, microseconds). Units: the client summary is emitted in SECONDS and the server gauge in MICROSECONDS. Every client expression here multiplies by 1000000 first, so both sides reach the axis in microseconds and are then divided by the Latency unit divisor.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "axisBorderShow": false,
            "axisCenteredZero": false,
